{
  /*
   * The project the TypeScript under Tests/ belongs to - the OpenStack e2e's
   * Ops/openstack-e2e/checks-run.ts and whole-path-template.ts, which run the
   * probe's and Common's own code - for editors and ESLint's typed linting
   * (projectService in eslint.config.js), which both take a file's nearest
   * tsconfig.json. Without this file the lookup walked on up to the
   * repository-root tsconfig.json, which has no "include": the two were
   * linted inside a program of the whole monorepo. That program outgrew the
   * 12 GB heap Scripts/Lint/LintByProject.js gives each ESLint process, and
   * js-lint failed on 2026-11-09 (ESLint killed by SIGABRT after 241 s; on
   * 2026-11-06 the same files had linted in 99 s). With this file they lint
   * in under a minute, in half a gigabyte.
   *
   * The repository root's compiler options, as before. Nothing builds from
   * here: checks-record.sh runs checks-run.ts with ts-node and
   * TS_NODE_PROJECT set to the probe's tsconfig.json, and whole-path.py
   * bundles whole-path-template.ts with esbuild, which reads the same
   * options through "extends" (the bundle is byte for byte what it was).
   */
  "extends": "../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["**/*.ts"]
}
